---
/**
 * Academic integrity, attribution and AI, on every IA tool page. The IB's
 * requirements are stated apart from the platform's recommendation, each
 * with the guide's page.
 */
import GuideLabel from './GuideLabel.astro';

interface Props {
  no: string;
}
const { no } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="ii" aria-labelledby={`ii-h-${no}`}>
  <header class="ii__head">
    <span class="ii__no" aria-hidden="true">{no}</span>
    <div>
      <h2 id={`ii-h-${no}`}><span class="sr-only">Section {no}: </span>Your own work</h2>
      <p class="ii__dek">What the IB requires of authentic work, and how the platform recommends using any outside help, including AI.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div class="ii__grid">
    <div class="ii__col">
      <p class="ce-labels"><GuideLabel kind="ib" /></p>
      <ul class="ii__list">
        <li>Work submitted for assessment must be your own, with the ideas and work of others fully acknowledged. <span class="ii__src">Guide, p. 4</span></li>
        <li>
          Acknowledge every source you use, in a standard referencing style used consistently: at least the author, the date of publication, the title and
          page numbers where they apply, and the date you accessed an electronic source. Mark quoted words as quotations. <span class="ii__src">Guide, pp. 4 to 5</span>
        </li>
        <li>Your teacher reads and advises on one draft, but does not edit it; the next version you hand in is the final one, and once submitted it cannot be retracted. <span class="ii__src">Guide, p. 51</span></li>
        <li>You confirm that the project is your authentic work, and the same work cannot be submitted for both the IA and the extended essay. <span class="ii__src">Guide, pp. 51 to 52</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="ii__col ii__col--rec">
      <p class="ce-labels"><GuideLabel kind="strategy" /></p>
      <ul class="ii__list">
        <li><b>Rules first.</b> Your school and the IB set the rules on AI tools. Ask your teacher what applies to you before you use one.</li>
        <li>
          <b>Help, not authorship.</b> If you use an AI tool at all, use it as you might a well-read friend: to explain an idea you have met, or to test your
          understanding. Do not let it choose your question, find or summarize your documents, analyse them, or write any part of the project.
        </li>
        <li><b>Say what you used.</b> If anything an AI tool produced appears in your work, acknowledge it as you would any other source, and keep a note of how you used it.</li>
        <li><b>Check everything.</b> An AI tool can be fluent and wrong. Every fact in your project should trace to a document or source you can cite.</li>
        <li><b>These tools.</b> Nothing on this platform writes your project. The tools check what you have planned and ask questions about it; your teacher guides you, and marks the work.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ii {
    padding: var(--sp-5);
    background: var(--surface-sheet);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--navy-900);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sheet);
  }

  .ii__head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .ii__no {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    color: var(--cobalt-text);
  }

  .ii__head h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-h3);
  }

  .ii__dek {
    margin-top: var(--sp-1);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .ii__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-6);
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .ii__list {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .ii__src {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .ii__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--sp-4);
    }

    .ii__head {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
